# sqlfluff setup

sqlfluff is a SQL linter, run on sql files by the pre-commit hook sqlfluff-lint.

The configuration is stored into this directory (and not at root of repository), so it does
not pollute the root directory. It is loaded thanks to the option

> --config dev/setup/sqlfluff/config

that is set into the file .pre-commit-config.yaml.

To run the linter manually, use:

> sqlfluff lint --config dev/setup/sqlfluff/config .

To fix violations automatically (check the diff after!), use:

> sqlfluff fix --config dev/setup/sqlfluff/config mydatabase.sql

Note that some sql files are excluded from the hook (see .pre-commit-config.yaml):
migration scripts and data files have a legacy SQL style that can not be rewritten.
